# Copy to backend/.env and fill in. Never commit the real file.
# AI: set ONE of these. Groq is used when GROQ_API_KEY is set, otherwise Claude.
# Groq keys (gsk_...) come from https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b      (must support strict structured outputs)
# DIXLAB_GROQ_MAX_TOKENS=4000         (reply cap; Groq's free tier allows ~8,000 tokens a minute)
# Claude keys (sk-ant-...) come from https://platform.claude.com
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# DIXLAB_AI_PROVIDER=groq             (force one provider when both keys are set: groq | anthropic)
# Optional
# DIXLAB_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
# DIXLAB_DB=data/dixlab.db
# DIXLAB_UPLOADS=uploads

# Email (confirmation codes, password resets, "Get in touch" messages). Pick ONE:
# a) SendLiberty (sendliberty.com): sends from a Gmail / Google Workspace account
#    you connect in its dashboard. API key from Dashboard -> API keys; the From
#    address must be that connected account. Used whenever both are set.
# SENDLIBERTY_API_KEY=
# SENDLIBERTY_FROM=Dixlab <yourname@gmail.com>
# b) Any SMTP provider. Without either, messages are only kept in each owner's Dixlab inbox.
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
# SMTP_FROM=Dixlab <no-reply@example.com>

# On the live server: strict defaults, and the API won't start with unsafe
# settings. Check first with:  .venv\Scripts\python -m app.prodcheck
# DIXLAB_ENV=production

# Admin dashboard (/admin): sign up in the app, then grant admin from backend/:
#   .venv\Scripts\python -m app.admin grant you@example.com
# No terminal on your host? Set this instead: that account becomes the FIRST admin
# once its email is confirmed. Ignored as soon as the site has any admin.
# DIXLAB_FIRST_ADMIN=you@example.com
# Admins must turn on two-step login first (default: on in production).
# DIXLAB_ADMIN_REQUIRE_2FA=true
# Interactive API docs at /docs (default: off in production).
# DIXLAB_API_DOCS=false

# Sessions: longest a login lasts, and how long unused before it ends.
# DIXLAB_SESSION_DAYS=30
# DIXLAB_SESSION_IDLE_DAYS=7

# Refuse passwords found in data breaches (Have I Been Pwned; only a 5-character
# hash prefix is sent).
# DIXLAB_PWNED_PASSWORD_CHECK=true

# Virus-scan uploads with a ClamAV daemon (uploads are refused if it's down).
# DIXLAB_CLAMAV=127.0.0.1:3310
# Brute-force limits (defaults shown):
# DIXLAB_LOGIN_FAILS_PER_EMAIL=8
# DIXLAB_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS_PER_IP=40
# DIXLAB_SIGNUPS_PER_IP=5
# DIXLAB_EVENT_RETENTION_DAYS=180

# Per-account limits (defaults shown).
# DIXLAB_STORAGE_MB_PER_USER=1024
# DIXLAB_MAX_PROJECTS_PER_USER=100
# Behind a reverse proxy (most hosts, e.g. Pxxl): how many proxies are in front
# of the app, so rate limits see visitors' real IPs. Leave 0 if unsure.
# DIXLAB_TRUST_PROXY_HOPS=1

# Plans and payments (Bachs, bachs.io). Free / Starter / Pro / Premium limits are on
# by default; set DIXLAB_PLAN_LIMITS=false to give every account everything (private test server).
# DIXLAB_PLAN_LIMITS=true
# DIXLAB_TRIAL_DAYS=14
# DIXLAB_REFUND_DAYS=14
# Prices are in the smallest unit: kobo for NGN, cents for USD. Naira and dollar
# prices are set separately (not converted). Defaults (yearly is about 20% off):
#   Starter  NGN 3,000 / 28,800    USD 3.99 / 38.30
#   Pro      NGN 6,000 / 57,600    USD 7.99 / 76.70
#   Premium  NGN 12,000 / 115,200  USD 14.99 / 143.90
# Override any of them: DIXLAB_PRICE_<PLAN>_<MONTHLY|YEARLY>_<NGN|USD>, e.g.
# DIXLAB_PRICE_STARTER_MONTHLY_NGN=300000
# DIXLAB_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY_USD=799
# USD prices must match the prices of your Bachs products.
# Secret API key from the Bachs Developer Portal (API keys): sk_sandbox_... for
# testing, sk_live_... on the real server. Never put it in the frontend.
# BACHS_API_KEY=
# Product ids (prod_...) of six recurring USD products you create in Bachs:
# BACHS_PRODUCT_STARTER_MONTHLY=
# BACHS_PRODUCT_STARTER_YEARLY=
# BACHS_PRODUCT_PRO_MONTHLY=
# BACHS_PRODUCT_PRO_YEARLY=
# BACHS_PRODUCT_PREMIUM_MONTHLY=
# BACHS_PRODUCT_PREMIUM_YEARLY=
# Naira: Bachs subscriptions bill USD cards only today, so naira plans are a
# one-off payment per month or year that people renew by paying again (no
# product needed). Once Bachs confirms naira recurring billing, create six NGN
# products, set BACHS_PRODUCT_<PLAN>_<INTERVAL>_NGN, and turn this on:
# DIXLAB_NGN_RECURRING=false
# Webhooks: in the Developer Portal add the destination
#   https://<your API domain>/api/billing/webhook
# (events: checkout.completed, customer.subscription.*, invoice.paid,
# invoice.payment_failed, refund.paid, refund.failed) and paste its signing secret here.
# BACHS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# DIXLAB_PUBLIC_URL (below) must be a public https address: Bachs refuses
# localhost return links, even in the sandbox.

# Account emails (confirm address, reset password) use the SMTP settings above.
# Where the frontend lives, for the links in those emails:
# DIXLAB_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:5173
# Local testing without an email server: print account emails in the backend
# terminal instead. NEVER on a real server (anyone reading logs could use the links).
# DIXLAB_MAIL_TO_LOG=true
